# ── Never commit ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# The signing secret and the Active Directory service-account password live
# here. Anyone holding JWT_SECRET can mint a token for any account, so this file
# belongs on each machine and nowhere else. server/.env.example is the template
# that IS committed.
# Everything .env-shaped, including the copies that get made around it —
# .env.bak (written by `npm run new-secret`), .env.local, .env.old, .env.save
# from an editor. A pattern listing only the exact name `.env` leaves every one
# of those committable, and .env.bak in particular holds the secret that was
# just rotated away.
.env
.env.*
*.env
!.env.example
!*.env.example

# The database, and the -wal/-shm files SQLite keeps beside it. Each deployment
# owns its own data; committing it would overwrite the server's records with
# whatever was last on a laptop.
server/data/

node_modules/

# ── Noise ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.log
npm-debug.log*
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
